  "title": "More ways to see, speak, and make video",
  "summary": "The API gained more ways to see, speak, and make video while the Pollen tools around it became easier to use and understand.\n\nThe model lineup widened across media. Chat gained Audio mode; `elevenflash` added a paid-only, low-latency speech option in alpha; and LTX-2 gained image-to-video input without changing its text-to-video path. Two Qwen vision options now separate non-reasoning work from larger thinking tasks. GPT-5.4 Mini and Mistral Small 4 joined the text-and-image lineup, while Seedream v4.0 and v4.5 Pro became discoverable again.\n\nDevelopers with publishable BYOP app keys gained an earnings view with charts, app-level figures, and CSV export. Enter also added automatic top-ups when a paid balance reaches 5 Pollen or less, plus access to payment and invoice controls. Pack bonuses were reduced, but checkout now records the grant offered at purchase. Updated policies and the FAQ explain wallets, app payments, and earnings; the 12-month inactivity clock for existing balances starts June 1, 2026.\n\nChat added a bring-your-own-Pollen-key dialog and clearer key errors. The homepage now explains the one-API approach, user-funded wallets, and optional developer earnings. Enter’s model descriptions, pricing units, and more consistent controls make the growing model list easier to navigate.\n\nQuest issues now state a fixed Pollen reward, goal, and acceptance criteria in the issue body. The merged-contribution payout path uses stable GitHub IDs and can find quests through PR-to-issue links, including sidebar links; missing links are flagged for review rather than silently skipped.",
